    { math: '1 · Kinship is society\'s operating system', note: 'Who counts as family decides inheritance, marriage rules, obligations, residence — in many societies THE organising institution, more than the state or market. Anthropology\'s technical heart since Morgan (1871).' },
    { math: '2 · Descent systems', note: 'Matrilineal (through mothers — Navajo, Akan), patrilineal (through fathers — most documented societies), bilateral (both — modern West). Each organises property, residence and identity differently — none is "natural"; all are designed.' },
